#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/autumn-equinox.tsx:55
msgid "The autumn equinox marks a moment of near-perfect balance, when day and night stand equal before the long shift toward darker evenings."
msgstr "The autumn equinox marks a moment of near-perfect balance, when day and night stand equal before the long shift toward darker evenings."

#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/halloween.tsx:32
msgid "The celebration grew from the ancient festival of Samhain and the later observance of All Hallows’ Eve, blending seasonal rites with remembrance of the dead."
msgstr "The celebration grew from the ancient festival of Samhain and the later observance of All Hallows’ Eve, blending seasonal rites with remembrance of the dead."

#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/autumn-equinox.tsx:92
msgid "The colour change in autumn leaves isn’t new pigment appearing — it’s the green chlorophyll withdrawing, revealing yellows and oranges that were there all along."
msgstr "The colour change in autumn leaves isn’t new pigment appearing — it’s the green chlorophyll withdrawing, revealing yellows and oranges that were there all along."

#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/black-hole.tsx:43
msgid "The dark center is the event horizon silhouette, while the bright ring is light from superheated material in the accretion flow around it."
msgstr "The dark center is the event horizon silhouette, while the bright ring is light from superheated material in the accretion flow around it."

#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/winter-solstice.tsx:88
msgid "The day after the solstice is only about a second longer — the shift is imperceptible at first, then gradually accelerates through January and February."
msgstr "The day after the solstice is only about a second longer — the shift is imperceptible at first, then gradually accelerates through January and February."

#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/eta-aquariids.tsx:84
msgid "The Eta Aquariids and the Orionids are sibling showers — both are born from Halley's Comet, but Earth crosses different parts of the debris trail six months apart."
msgstr "The Eta Aquariids and the Orionids are sibling showers — both are born from Halley's Comet, but Earth crosses different parts of the debris trail six months apart."

#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/eta-aquariids.tsx:52
msgid "The Eta Aquariids are a major meteor shower formed from the debris of Halley’s Comet."
msgstr "The Eta Aquariids are a major meteor shower formed from the debris of Halley’s Comet."

#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/total-lunar-eclipse.tsx:46
msgid "The event unfolds gradually, often lasting several hours from beginning to end."
msgstr "The event unfolds gradually, often lasting several hours from beginning to end."

#: src/features/seasonal-events/definitions/total-lunar-eclipse.tsx:96
msgid "The exact shade of red depends on what's in Earth's atmosphere at the time. After major volcanic eruptions, the Moon can turn an especially dark, almost brownish red."
msgstr "The exact shade of red depends on what's in Earth's atmosphere at the time. After major volcanic eruptions, the Moon can turn an especially dark, almost brownish red."

